{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BindingIsovectorChiralResidue","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BindingIsovectorChiralResidue","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.binding_isovector_A_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.binding_isovector_A_independent","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BindingIsovectorChiralResidue.lean#L66-L78","doc":"**Corollary (A-independence of `b`).** The binding isovector coefficient does\nnot depend on `A`: for any two mass numbers, the same chiral weight `κ` governs\nthe mirror difference. Concretely, the per-`(Z−N)` slope is `2κ` at every `A`\n(here shown as the mirror difference depending only on `κ` and `Z−N`, not on\n`Z+N`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.binding_isovector_mirror_from_chiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.binding_isovector_mirror_from_chiral","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BindingIsovectorChiralResidue.lean#L54-L64","doc":"**Conditional (proved; the chiral identification is the hypothesis).** Given\nthe keystone chiral identification, the binding isovector mirror difference is\n`4·κ·(Z−N)` — **A-independent**, with the per-`T₃` coefficient `b = 4κ` fixed by\nthe keystone chiral weight `κ`. This routes the binding isovector closure into the\nSAME single open conjecture as the W_λ keystone (`BWVacuumRowIsHecke`): once `κ`\nis derived there, the binding `b` follows, and the test `residual b → 0` becomes\na binding-side check on the keystone. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:isovector-chiral-residue","label":"prop:isovector-chiral-residue","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-mass-binding-algorithms/mba-sidecar-isovector-chiral-residue.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaChiralBinding.bindingOdd_eq_chiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaChiralBinding.bindingOdd_eq_chiral","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BindingIsovectorChiralResidue.lean#L52-L52","doc":"**Identification (conjectural content).** The binding odd part is the chiral\nresidue carried by the writhe's isovector part `2(Z−N)` (`writhe = 4Z = 2A +\n2(Z−N)`, the A-independent isovector slope), weight `κ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaChiralBinding.bindingOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaChiralBinding.bindingOdd","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BindingIsovectorChiralResidue.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The binding residual's isovector (bar-odd) part, as a function of `(Z, N)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaChiralBinding.kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaChiralBinding.kappa","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BindingIsovectorChiralResidue.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The chiral-residue weight from the keystone W_λ Plancherel measure\n`μ(λ)=d_q²/D²` (chiral part). Open value ⟶ `BWVacuumRowIsHecke`; never a fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaChiralBinding.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaChiralBinding.mk","kind":"ctor","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BindingIsovectorChiralResidue.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaChiralBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaChiralBinding","kind":"class","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BindingIsovectorChiralResidue.lean#L33-L52","doc":"**§3b-cond conditional class — the keystone-shared chiral identification.**\nThe Δ_λ binding residual's isovector (bar-odd) part is the chiral residue of the\nW_λ Plancherel measure, carried by the writhe's isovector part `2(Z−N)` with an\n**A-independent** chiral weight `κ`.\n\nThe conjectural content is `bindingOdd_eq_chiral` — a parameter-quantified\nidentification (not `True`, not the downstream conclusion): the binding's odd\npart equals `κ·2(Z−N)`, with `κ` the chiral-residue weight of `μ(λ)=d_q²/D²`. Its\nopen value routes to the keystone's single open conjecture `BWVacuumRowIsHecke`;\nno instance is fabricated (the value stays open, gated, unfit). ","signatureChunk":0}]}